{
  "about": "Change case on both phones (Android TextCase, iOS ChangeCase): each row's words as they read, the design's language, the UTF-16 range changed (start, end; null for all of the words) and what each of the four makes of it. Each letter is cased on its own in the language's locale. Title Case: a letter starts a word when the character before it is not a letter, a digit or an apostrophe (' or ’); it is upper case and every other letter lower case. Sentence case: every letter lower case but the first of the words, of each line, and the first after '.', '!' or '?' and then a space; a digit before any letter starts nothing. Where words and sentences start is read from all of the words, not only the range. `caps` gives boxes with a span's \"caps\" and the words they are drawn as.",
